A cut of FFmpeg n7.1.1 (commit db69d06eeeab4f46da15030a80d539efb4503ca8) holding only the decoders rct3pp
needs: Windows Media Audio 1 and 2 (the game's music and sounds) and Windows Media Video 9, WMV3 (the first
release's startup movies).
https://ffmpeg.org/
Licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License version 2.1 or later; see COPYING.LGPLv2.1.

How it was cut: FFmpeg's own configure, for portable C only, with

  ./configure --disable-everything --disable-programs --disable-doc --disable-network --disable-autodetect
      --disable-asm --disable-x86asm --disable-inline-asm --disable-pthreads --disable-avdevice
      --disable-avformat --disable-swscale --disable-swresample --disable-avfilter --disable-iconv
      --enable-decoder=wmv3,wmav1,wmav2 --disable-hwaccels --disable-debug --enable-small

then libavcodec and libavutil built, and cut further:

- Only the decoders' own files are kept, and the few general ones they call that are small: memory, buffers,
  frames, picture and sample sizes, the float transforms, fractions. Their sources are in sources.txt.
  Everything those sources include came along. All of it is unmodified from the tag, laid out as in
  FFmpeg's tree.
- The rest of what they call is written small in rct3_libav.c: logging (dropped), the pixel format table
  (planar 4:2:0 only), channel layouts (plain mono and stereo), getting a frame's buffer and its format
  (one thread, no hardware decoding), start codes, the block compare error concealment uses, and the
  other inverse transforms (all the default one). FFmpeg's open, send and receive are replaced by
  rct3_codec.c, which sets a decoder's context up with the defaults these decoders read and calls the
  decoder directly.
- libavcodec/aac_scalefactor.c holds the two tables of aactab.c the WMA decoder uses, cut out of that file
  unchanged.

Generated by that configure run, kept with only the defines the files here use:
  config.h config_components.h libavutil/avconfig.h
config.h was made on x86-64 Linux with GCC; with assembly off it only names what the C library offers.

Written for rct3pp, LGPL-2.1-or-later:
  rct3_wma.h rct3_wma.c      open a WMA decoder for a stream's format, decode a packet
  rct3_wmv.h rct3_wmv.c      open a WMV3 decoder for a stream's format, decode a frame to Y, U and V planes
  rct3_codec.h rct3_codec.c  a decoder's context, started, fed and freed
  rct3_libav.c               the stand-ins above

It is compiled as C17 into the rct3pp binary (nob.cpp, compile_audio, which builds what sources.txt lists);
nothing of FFmpeg is linked from the system. To cut it again for another tag, repeat the steps above: build
a program that decodes through rct3_wma and rct3_wmv against the full libraries, keep the files it reaches,
and let the linker's undefined symbols say what rct3_libav.c must still provide.
